# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so without this every clone on
# a teammate's Windows machine rewrites the hook scripts to CRLF. git-bash then
# dies on the stray CR ("$'\r': command not found", "set: pipefail\r: invalid
# option name") and, because SessionStart is a blocking hook, the CLI never
# becomes ready.
#
# hooks/run-hook.cmd is a cmd/sh polyglot: macOS executes the same file through
# /bin/sh, so it must stay LF too even though it is a .cmd. It contains no
# parenthesised if/for block and no `goto`, which are the only constructs
# cmd.exe actually mis-parses in an LF-only batch file.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.cmd  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
